@crnlchez1234-afk @jamilahmadzai @mnn31 thanks for your work here so far! I need to make a correction from the original issue description.

I had previously written that paulis should be added before and after the circuit (effectively doing some sort of twirling operation), but this does not correctly implement the debiasing protocol as described in the paper. Instead the circuit $C$ needs to be prepended with a permutation of the qubits $C\to \pi C$ where $\pi:[n]\to[n]$ is a permutation of the $n$ qubits. The post-processing for each circuit should then be "unscrambling" $\pi$ before combining. Each variant should get a different permutation as well.

Apologies for not catching this earlier. Let me know if you have any questions in the meantime! Please ping me when you a ready for a review on your PR once you make these changes.

@natestemen  Hi! I opened a PR for this: #3053 
The notebook walks through preparing |1_L 0_L> with the [[4,2,2]] encoding circuit (4-qubit GHZ + a logical X), measuring the XXXX/ZZZZ syndromes with two ancillas, then comparing four cases under 2% local depolarizing noise: ideal, noisy unmitigated, mitiq.rem.post_select only, and post-selection combined with mitiq.zne.execute_with_zne (Richardson extrapolation). The discussion section covers the shot-discarding overhead from post-selection, as suggested in the issue.
I noticed there's already an open PR (#3025) that also references this issue as part of a larger multi-issue PR — happy to adjust scope or defer if that one's the preferred direction, just wanted to put this together since the deliverable was pretty clearly scoped. looking forward to your review
